WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.440
After starting a post,

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.740
look at the Queue tab

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.020
in Post to Market.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:05.500
Read the status

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.540
on each vehicle.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.100
Preparing or processing means

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.460
the work is still underway.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:12.560
Published means that

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.100
vehicle has finished posting.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.270
If a row says Failed,

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.630
read its message before

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:18.970
starting anything again.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:20.870
Here's a batch with two

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:21.920
published and four

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:22.940
still remaining.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.520
That isn't a completed

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.580
six-vehicle batch.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.990
Keep the computer

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.710
online and AutoLander

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.930
running while it works.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.690
You can do other tasks

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.370
and check back; you don't

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.540
need to watch every step.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.000
To review listings

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
you've posted, click Posted

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.640
to FB beside Queue.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.980
Find the vehicle

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.000
you want to check.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.320
You can also open

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.490
your Facebook Marketplace

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.660
listings and check

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.940
the matching vehicle there.

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.630
Confirm its price,

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:50.270
description and availability,

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.090
rather than relying only

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.750
on a total in AutoLander.

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.050
If a vehicle

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.070
is still waiting,

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.370
don't add it again just

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.670
because it's taking a while.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.880
Check the existing job first.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.620
Pause on this example.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.540
Which vehicles are done,

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.860
which are still working,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.880
and which message

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.080
would need your attention?
